Playing a Valk.  So far...

- my dog fell into a pit on level two and died

- haven't seen a cat or dog (or an egg, etc.) since, and have no other
ways of gaining a new pet

- naturally, I've found a half-dozen tripe rations

- Minetown's altar was cross-aligned

- no other altars yet (I'm several levels past the Oracle)

- no floating eyes have left corpses.  So no telepathy.

- did manage to find three rust traps.  The hard way.

- dipped for Excalibur.  The first fountain cursed my long sword, then
rusted it, then rusted it some more, then dried up.  Didn't find any
more fountains until Oracle (I know, always have several fountains
before you dip...this is my fault)

- Oh, and when I got to the Oracle, I nearly died due to the endless
stream of snakes

- no poison resistance yet so my strength was down to 14 following
that misadventure

- which means I'm burdened

- be nice if I found a chest, but the only one is on Dlvl 1, which is
the least convenient stash of all time.  I should move it down, but of
course, I'm already burdened...

- no rings.  One wand of speed monster.  Oh, and a dozen spellbooks,
naturally.

- other than Minetown, found one shop: a four-square used armor
dealership with nothing interesting

- Minetown had two delicatessans, Izchak's, and no other shops.
Great.

- only seen one unicorn, and it was lawful.  So no horn.  Too bad
because I could really use a STR restore.

- found various scrolls, but no identify

- so (since I have no horn) I have no idea what all these potions are
and I'm not brave enough to blindly quaff

- and likewise I have no means of pet-testing all of these lovely
ranged weapons I've found, so I've been making a list of nymphs and
leprechauns to go back for

- found a magic lamp down in the minds and altar-BUC-tested it.
Blessed!  Sweet!  Eagerly rubbed it and..."You freed me!"  Just can't
catch a break.

I assume the RNG will make all of this up to me by putting a wand of
wishing on the next level...


